{
  "algorithm": "ridge",
  "name": "Ridge Regression",
  "description": "Linear model with L2 penalty on standardised inputs. Fast and transparent; extrapolates linearly.",
  "preprocessing": "`Pipeline`: ColumnTransformer (numeric features \u2192 median imputation fitted on the training rows, with a binary missing-indicator column per feature, then StandardScaler; categorical features (the market identifier) \u2192 one-hot encoding, unknown categories ignored) \u2192 `Ridge(alpha)`. Linear, so it extrapolates beyond the training range and can predict below zero for small markets. With `log_target`, the estimator is wrapped in `TransformedTargetRegressor(log1p, expm1)`; every metric is reported in guests. With the `floor_zero` policy the pipeline is wrapped in `NonNegative`, which floors predictions at 0 (raw negatives are still counted in the metadata).",
